{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "MAT",
  "chapter": 20,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the kingdom of heaven is like to a man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a householder, who went out early in the morning to hire laborers into his vineyard.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he had agreed with the laborers for a penny a day, he sent them into his vineyard.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he went out about the third hour, and saw others standing idle in the market-place,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And said to them, Go ye also into the vineyard; and whatever is right, I will give you. And they departed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Again he went out about the sixth and ninth hour, and did likewise.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And about the eleventh hour he went out, and found others standing idle, and saith to them, Why stand ye here all the day idle?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They say to him, Because no man hath hired us. He saith to them, Go ye also into the vineyard; and whatever is right, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall ye receive.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So when evening was come, the lord of the vineyard saith to his steward, Call the laborers, and give them ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hire, beginning from the last to the first.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when they came that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were hired",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " about the eleventh hour, they received every man a penny.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But when the first came, they supposed that they should receive more; and they likewise received every man a penny.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when they had received ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", they murmured against the master of the house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Saying, These last have wrought ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " one hour, and thou hast made them equal to us, who have borne the burden and heat of the day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he answered one of them, and said, Friend, I do thee no wrong: didst thou not agree with me for a penny?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thine, and depart: I will give to this last, even as to thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is it not lawful for me to do what I will with my own? is thy eye evil because I am good?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So the last shall be first, and the first last: for many are called, but few chosen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jesus going up to Jerusalem, took the twelve disciples apart in the way, and said to them,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, we go up to Jerusalem; and the Son of man will be betrayed to the chief priests, and to the scribes, and they will condemn him to death,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And will deliver him to the Gentiles to mock, and to scourge, and to crucify ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": and the third day he will rise again.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then came to him the mother of Zebedee's children, with her sons, worshiping ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and desiring a certain thing of him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said to her, What wilt thou: She saith to him, Grant that these my two sons may sit, the one on thy right hand, and the other on the left in thy kingdom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Jesus answered and said, Ye know not what ye ask. Are ye able to drink of the cup that I shall drink of, and to be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with? They say to him, We are able.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he saith to them, Ye shall drink indeed of my cup, and be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with: but to sit on my right hand, and on my left, is not mine to give, but ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it shall be given",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to them for whom it is prepared by my Father.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when the ten heard ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", they were moved with indignation against the two brethren.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Jesus called them ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and said, Ye know that the princes of the Gentiles exercise dominion over them, and they that are great exercise authority upon them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But it shall not be so among you: but whoever will be great among you, let him be your minister;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And whoever will be chief among you, let him be your servant:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even as the Son of man came not to be ministered to, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And as they departed from Jericho, a great multitude followed him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And behold, two blind men sitting by the way-side, when they heard that Jesus passed by, cried out, saying, Have mercy on us, O Lord, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thou",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " son of David.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the multitude rebuked them, that they should hold their peace: but they cried the more, saying, Have mercy on us, O Lord, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thou",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " son of David.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jesus stood still, and called them, and said, What will ye that I shall do to you?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They say to him, Lord, that our eyes may be opened.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.20.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.20.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So Jesus had compassion ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "on them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and touched their eyes: and immediately their eyes received sight, and they followed him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
